==============================================================================================================
B. The layered conduction model
==============================================================================================================
lateral period 24 pitches = 89.3 mm, 288 x 288 samples of 0.310 mm
checkerboard     : 16 shires vs 16; commutated with its complement; contrast = on ROI minus its reference ROIs, averaged over 8 pair(s)
one shire        : 1 shires vs 0; S21 on/off; contrast = on ROI minus its reference ROIs, averaged over 1 pair(s)
2x2 block moving : 4 shires vs 4; NE block <-> SW block, commutated (the MAP pair); contrast = on ROI minus its reference ROIs, averaged over 4 pair(s)
half die         : 18 shires vs 14; west half <-> east half, commutated; contrast = on ROI minus its reference ROIs, averaged over 5 pair(s)
self-checks: q = 0 mode equals the series-parallel resistances; f -> 0 equals steady state: ok
