Columns: one live frame; a difference image of two settled states, 1 s (25 frames) of each; lock-in 1 min, 10 min, 1 h.  "<0.01" = below 10 kHz; ">600" = not at 600 MHz.  Other kernels need 1/x the power: int8 randn or fp32 ones x0.37-0.39, so about 2.6 times the clock.  Only the mean switching power per shire counts, so "clock only" is also a duty cycle at 600 MHz: x MHz = the kernel busy x/600 of the time.
